# EtMultiLineChart

The UI kit's compare chart: multiple line series rendered on one unified y-domain so the lines are visually comparable. Built for the User/SP page "compare performance" design (Figma DS — React, general chart node) and consumed by feature compare flows (e.g. the compare bottom sheet).

## Usage

```tsx
const selectedValue = useSharedValue(0);
const { colors } = useEtoroTheme();

<EtMultiLineChart
  series={[
    { data: primarySeries, color: colors.verdictPositive600 }, // primary — drives the cursor
    { data: benchmarkSeries, color: colors.accentB700 },
    { data: peerSeries, color: colors.accentD700 },
    { data: secondPeerSeries, color: colors.accentF700 },
  ]}
  selectedValue={selectedValue}
  yAxisTickCount={4}
  yAxisTickFormat={(value) => `${Math.round(value)}%`}
  onCursorDataChange={(cursorData) => setHeader(cursorData)}
/>
```

